jobs.description:
What will you do?

Do you have an affinity for technology or experience in technical production, and are you handy with practical work? Are you also looking for a long-term job opportunity? Then look no further!

As a Field Service Technician, you will visit various organizations, ranging from large government institutions and universities to hospitals. The work requires specialized skills, for which you will receive internal training.

Your responsibilities include:

- Maintenance and renovation of air handling systems;
- Cleaning and gas-free preparation of installations within the chemical industry;
- Collaborating with various clients to ensure technical installations function optimally.

Who are you?

In addition to an interest in technology and technical insight, you have:

- A VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- A valid Category B driving license;
- Strong communication skills, customer friendliness, and initiative;
- Good command of the English and/or Dutch language.

As an Order Planner, you are the key link between customers, production, purchasing, customer service, and our external production partners. You ensure that orders are processed correctly, schedules are accurate, and delivery commitments are met.

What will you do?

- Process and review customer orders.
- Coordinate and confirm delivery dates.
- Prepare and maintain production and delivery schedules.
- Adjust schedules in response to changes in demand, capacity, or material availability.
- Communicate daily with production, purchasing, customer service, and external partners.
- Monitor orders and deliveries and make adjustments where necessary.

This position is available on both a part-time and full-time basis. You will work regular daytime hours, from 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM.

- MBO-level education and working experience;
- Experience in order planning is a plus, but not a requirement;
- Experience with ERP systems (e.g. Navision) and proficient in using Excel;
- Accurate, well-organized, and strong communication skills;
- A practical mindset and the ability to maintain an overview in a dynamic environment;
- Good command of English.

Wolfram Chain is looking for a motivated Class C truck driver for a transport company that supplies catering and hospitality businesses, based in Berkel en Rodenrijs.You will work closely with a direct colleague, get to know many regular customers, and at the end of the day, you can enjoy a hot meal at the office for a small fee.Ready for a new challenge? Check out this vacancy or get in touch with us!

Functieomschrijving:
What you will do:As a Class C truck driver for this company, your working days will be focused on supplying hospitality businesses. Your responsibilities include:
• Representing the company and having a friendly conversation with customers;
• Working from Monday to Friday;
• You will deliver food and drinks;
• Want to work extra hours? That's possible. Prefer to work four days a week? That's possible too.

Functievereisten:
What we expect from you as a driver:
• You have a valid Class C or CE driving licence;
• You are physically fit and comfortable performing physically demanding tasks;
• You have a good command of either Dutch or English.

Arbeidsvoorwaarden:
What you can expect in return:
• A gross monthly salary between €3,000 and €5,000;
• Overtime paid at 130%, plus an ADV allowance;
• A good pension scheme in accordance with the collective labour agreement (CAO);
• 24 paid vacation days;
• The opportunity to follow internal training courses;
• Getting your class CE license for free;
• A fresh, hot meal every day at the office for just €2.50;
• A permanent contract upon good performance.
Interested?Apply now!

